Production-acceptance follow-through (no algorithm redesign):

Subject-side precision safety (was a proven gap): a distance tier now requires the
SUBJECT's own coordinate to be precise enough too, not only the comparable's. A
subject with a CITY/NEIGHBORHOOD/unknown-precision coordinate can no longer reach
≤300m/≤700m/street/building — its own distance would be meaningless. This also
removes the asking-only radius path at its source (a geocoded-but-imprecise subject
falls to city/sold-anchored instead of an asking-only radius subset). ValuationInput
carries locationResolution; the service passes the subject property's geocode
resolution. Regression tests added; existing tier tests updated for the new rule.

Broker evidence UI (previously deferred): a plain-Hebrew evidence module on the
result screen — "הערכת שווי מבוססת/ראשונית", what it's based on (sold vs asking vs
office), confidence label, and an honest asking-only / city-only disclosure. No
engine internals (no UUID/sourceTable/reason codes).

Seller report: natural low-evidence wording ("הערכת השווי ראשונית…") when the
estimate leans on asking prices or confidence is low; standard wording otherwise.

